  "summary": "An invitation-only group that Alfred Stieglitz formed on 17 February 1902. It promoted photography as a fine art and pictorialism in particular. It ran the Little Galleries from 1905. Stieglitz dissolved it in 1917, when it existed in name only. Wikipedia calls it the American counterpart to the Linked Ring.",
